[[0,23689,0,11,0,11,"2014-08-26T08:12:00","BadMoonRising","",[],"","Police shoot another teenager","http://www.kctv5.com/story/26355241/ottawa-police-involved-in-shooting","news"],[1,21256,0,0,0,0,"2014-08-27T05:39:00","LordTronicus","",[],"<p>Is there not some type of monitoring system put in place for someone who just tried to overdose? Where I live I'm pretty sure there is a 48 hour hold for suicide watch, after a person tries to kill themselves.</p>"],[2,21270,21256,0,0,0,"2014-08-28T04:16:00","BadMoonRising","",[],"<p>Where do you live, may I ask?</p>"],[3,21387,21270,0,0,0,"2014-08-29T19:05:00","LordTronicus","",[],"<p>Toronto, Canada.</p>"],[4,21399,21387,1,0,1,"2014-08-30T05:56:00","BadMoonRising","",[],"<p>I was guessing it wasn't america, lol</p>"],[1,21332,0,2,0,2,"2014-08-28T18:09:00","Gingeree","",[],"<p>Yet another tragic data point that shows the police <em>really</em> need better training on how to de-escalate and handle mentally ill persons. This is bullshit. Getting tired of the &quot;shoot first, ask questions&quot; cowboy approach to policing these days. Of course, it'll take tax money to do it, and nobody wants to pay for it. So I guess we'll just sit around at yet another vigil and check &quot;NO&quot; on the ballot box for these sorts of initiatives. That's what history suggests, at least.</p>"]]
